# One line-ending rule for every platform: LF in the repository and LF in the
# working tree. Without it a Windows checkout or a Windows gate run can leave
# CRLF in tracked files (issue #85). Must come first: later lines refine it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The elaboration dumps are machine-read by check_elaboration_drift.py and by
# nothing else. `-diff` renders a migration as one `Bin` line instead of 42,000
# unreviewable ones, while leaving the bytes as plain text so git can still
# zlib and delta them -- which committing them gzipped would have prevented.
docs/status/elab-baseline-*.json -diff
